---
layout: layout.njk
---
{#
  POST LAYOUT
  ===========
  Every file in src/posts/ that has "layout: post.njk" in its front matter
  gets wrapped in this template automatically. This is the file that
  turns your plain writing into a fully-styled page matching the site.

  Front matter fields this template reads:
    title           - required. The post headline.
    date            - required. Used for sorting and the byline date.
    category        - required. Which of the 6 categories this belongs to.
                       Must exactly match one of: questioning-and-thought,
                       deprogramming-and-education, the-expanse,
                       communication-and-empathy, meaningful-action, social
    author          - optional. Shows in the byline. Defaults to "FWYM".
    featuredImage    - optional. Large image shown at the top of the post.
    featuredImageAlt - the text description of that image, for screen
                       readers. If featuredImage is set, fill this in.
    excerpt          - optional. Short teaser text (not shown on the post
                       itself, but available for category-listing cards).
    relatedPosts      - optional. A list of other posts' URLs to link at
                       the bottom, e.g. "/some-post-slug/". If left out
                       entirely, this template automatically picks the 3
                       most recent OTHER posts from the same category.
#}
{#
  Every post gets a two-column layout on desktop: the article on the
  left (2/3 width) and an aside on the right (1/3 width) — either a
  post's own custom "noteAside" content, or, when a post doesn't define
  one, the site's default donation/contributor boxes (sidebar-boxes.njk).
  This matches the same isBoxesAside pattern used for the featured post
  on category pages, including the responsive behavior: on mobile, the
  default donation boxes move out of the inline column (hidden there)
  and reappear once, lower down, inside the footer — right after
  "Related posts" — so visitors reach the actual article without
  scrolling past a donation pitch first. A post's own custom noteAside
  content (like the "Is it Really Brainwashing?" note) is NOT part of
  that swap — it stays inline in its own column always, on both mobile
  and desktop, same as before.
#}
{% set isBoxesAside = (not noteAside) or noteAsideClass == "column" %}
{#
  "Tactic entry" styling: the short glossary-style write-ups in the
  deprogramming-and-education category (Fear, Lying, Micro Targeting,
  etc.) get a distinct in-page treatment — the image floats so text
  wraps beside it instead of stacking below with dead space, extra
  breathing room under the title, and a drop cap on the opening
  paragraph. This is scoped ONLY to that category via the
  "tactic-entry" class below; every other post/category keeps the
  normal stacked-image layout untouched.
#}
{% set isTacticEntry = category == "deprogramming-and-education" %}
<div class="content">
	<section>
		<div class="column {{ isTacticEntry and 'tactic-entry' or '' }}" style="margin-top:0; flex: {{ mainColumnFlex or (isBoxesAside and '2' or '1') }};">
			<h1 style="font-size: 6vmax;">{{ title }}</h1>

			{% if featuredImage %}
				<img src="{{ featuredImage | url }}" alt="{{ featuredImageAlt or '' }}">
			{% endif %}

			{{ content | safe }}
		</div>

		<div class="column {{ isBoxesAside and 'post-sidebar' or (noteAsideClass or 'secondary-p') }}" style="flex: {{ noteAsideFlex or '1' }};">
			{% if noteAside %}
				{{ noteAside | fixPaths | safe }}
			{% else %}
				{% include "sidebar-boxes.njk" %}
			{% endif %}
		</div>
	</section>


	{% if extraSection %}
		{{ extraSection | fixPaths | safe }}
	{% endif %}
</div>

{#
  RELATED POSTS
  =============
  If the post's front matter includes a manual "relatedPosts" list (a list
  of URLs, e.g. "/some-post-slug/"), those exact posts are shown, in the
  order listed. Otherwise, this automatically shows the 3 most recent
  OTHER posts sharing this post's category. Either way, it renders using
  the site's real related-posts styling (.yarpp-related class).
#}
{% if relatedPosts %}
  {% set related = collections.allPosts | relatedByUrls(relatedPosts) %}
{% else %}
  {% set related = collections[category] | relatedByCategory(page.url) %}
{% endif %}

{% if related.length > 0 %}
<div class="yarpp-related">
	<h3>Related posts:</h3>
	<div class="yarpp-thumbnails-horizontal">
		{% for item in related %}
			<a class="yarpp-thumbnail" href="{{ item.url | url }}">
				{% if item.data.featuredImage %}
					<img src="{{ item.data.featuredImage | url }}" alt="">
				{% endif %}
				<span class="yarpp-thumbnail-title">{{ item.data.title }}</span>
			</a>
		{% endfor %}
	</div>
</div>
{% endif %}
